      "text": "To determine the sum of the digits of the product of \\(24_7\\) and \\(30_7\\) in base seven, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert the base 7 numbers to base 10.\n2. Multiply the two base 10 numbers.\n3. Convert the product from base 10 back to base 7.\n4. Sum the digits of the base 7 product.\n\n**Step 1: Convert the base 7 numbers to base 10.**\n\nThe number \\(24_7\\) in base 10 is:\n\\[\n2 \\cdot 7^1 + 4 \\cdot 7^0 = 2 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot 1 = 14 + 4 = 18\n\\]\nThe number \\(30_7\\) in base 10 is:\n\\[\n3 \\cdot 7^1 + 0 \\cdot 7^0 = 3 \\cdot 7 + 0 \\cdot 1 = 21 + 0 = 21\n\\]\n\n**Step 2: Multiply the two base 10 numbers.**\n\nThe product of 18 and 21 in base 10 is:\n\\[\n18 \\cdot 21 = 378\n\\]\n\n**Step 3: Convert the product from base 10 back to base 7.**\n\nTo convert 378 from base 10 to base 7, we repeatedly divide by 7 and keep track of the remainders:\n\\[\n378 \\div 7 = 54 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 0\n\\]\n\\[\n54 \\div 7 = 7 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 5\n\\]\n\\[\n7 \\div 7 = 1 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 0\n\\]\n\\[\n1 \\div 7 = 0 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 1\n\\]\nReading the remainders from bottom to top, we get \\(1050_7\\).\n\n**Step 4: Sum the digits of the base 7 product.**\n\nThe digits of \\(1050_7\\) are 1, 0, 5, and 0. The sum of these digits is:\n\\[\n1 + 0 + 5 + 0 = 6\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the base seven sum of the digits of the product is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{6}\n\\]",
